.TH DAQ-OPEN-TUNNELS 1 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
daq-open-tunnels \- open, list and tear down the shifter SSH tunnels
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B daq-open-tunnels
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIstate\fR]
[\fB\-b\fR \fIbase\fR]
[\fB\-u\fR \fIuser\fR]
[\fB\-\-gui\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
{\fBopen\fR|\fBkill\fR|\fBlist\fR}
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B daq-open-tunnels
manages the SSH local forwards described in \fIconfig/tunnels.yaml\fR.
Each running tunnel is recorded in a state file so that \fBlist\fR and
\fBkill\fR can find it again from a later shell.
.PP
The local port of a tunnel is
.PP
.RS
.nf
base_port + port
.fi
.RE
.PP
where \fIport\fR is the entry's offset and \fIbase_port\fR defaults to
the caller's uid plus 973 (Mu2e is E-973). Deriving it from the uid
keeps concurrent users on a shared shifter machine out of each other's
way without any coordination.
.PP
Before opening anything, the resolved local ports are checked for
collisions. Two entries landing on one port cannot both be forwarded,
and because \fBExitOnForwardFailure\fR is set the second ssh simply
dies; a warning names the entries involved rather than leaving that to
be discovered later.
.PP
This command manages the tunnels defined in YAML. For the fixed set of
control-room GUI forwards, use
.BR daq-tunnels.sh (1)
instead.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B open
Start every tunnel in the configuration. Tunnels already recorded and
alive are left running and reported.
.TP
.B kill
Send \fBSIGTERM\fR to every recorded tunnel and rewrite the state file
with whatever survived.
.TP
.B list
Show each recorded tunnel with its pid, host, local port and whether
the process is still alive. This is the default action.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then .env file, then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Tunnel definitions to read. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_TUNNELS\fR.
Default: the first \fItunnels.yaml\fR on the config search path.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-state\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Where running tunnels are recorded. Environment:
\fBMU2EDAQ_TUNNEL_STATE\fR. Default: \fI~/.mu2edaq/open_tunnels\fR.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-base\-port " " \fIN\fR
Local port base. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_TUNNEL_BASE_PORT\fR. Default:
uid + 973.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR
Override the ssh username for every tunnel, ignoring the per-entry
\fBusername\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-gui
With \fBlist\fR, show the tunnels in a Qt dialog instead of on the
terminal. Requires PyQt5, which
.BR bootstrap.sh (1)
installs unless \fB\-\-no\-gui\fR was used. PyQt is imported only when
this flag is given, so the rest of the command works on a text-only
session.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the ssh command lines and change nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the package version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Each entry of \fItunnels.yaml\fR takes:
.TP
.B hostname
Host to ssh to. Required.
.TP
.B port
Port offset, added to the base port. Required.
.TP
.B username
SSH user. Defaults to \fB$USER\fR.
.TP
.B remote
Host the far end of the forward connects to. Defaults to
\fIlocalhost\fR.
.TP
.B jump
ProxyJump host. Optional.
.TP
.B label
Name shown by \fBlist\fR. Optional.
.PP
A bare list of entries is accepted as well as a mapping with a
\fBtunnels:\fR key, and because JSON is valid YAML the historical
\fItunnels.json\fR still loads.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/tunnels.yaml
Tunnel definitions.
.TP
.I ~/.mu2edaq/open_tunnels
Recorded tunnels, as \fBpid, hostname, username, local_port, label\fR.
The older four-field format without \fBlabel\fR is still read.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, and 1 when the configuration cannot be read or
ssh cannot be started. With \fB\-\-gui\fR, 1 also means PyQt5 is not
installed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open every tunnel and check it came up:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-open-tunnels open
daq-open-tunnels list
.fi
.RE
.PP
See the command lines without connecting:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-open-tunnels --dry-run open
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use a fixed port base, so the ports are the same for everyone:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-open-tunnels --base-port 1973 open
.fi
.RE
.PP
Close them:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-open-tunnels kill
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR daq-tunnels.sh (1),
.BR start-novnc-connection.sh (1),
.BR ssh (1)
